cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "PolicyJEV: a pre-registered comparison of zero-shot TypeSafe JEV with trained baselines on toxic-comment classification, with a moderation policy layer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rana
    given-names: Muhammad Abbas
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AbbasRana001/PolicyJEV"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered comparison of zero-shot TypeSafe JEV (jev-1.13.0) with a TF-IDF
  logistic regression and a fine-tuned DistilBERT on the Jigsaw Toxic Comment
  Classification Challenge test set (63,978 comments), followed by an evaluation of
  a three-way moderation policy (allow, human review, action) with thresholds fixed
  on validation data. On test, JEV has the lowest mean average precision of the
  three systems, and the validation targets for the policy did not hold on test for
  any system. The repository contains the protocol, frozen-file manifest, metrics,
  predictions, policy engine and a React and FastAPI console. It contains no comment text.
keywords:
  - toxicity classification
  - content moderation
  - zero-shot classification
  - pre-registration
  - calibration
  - reproducible research
